-- The keyed hop: rel;unique⁻¹. Twin of 015-keyed-hop.bqn. (was s60-keyed-hop)
-- A guild with prime ids: mentor and targets name entities by id through `unique id`, never by row position. One Cursed guildmate despawns mid-program, and every hop after it must still resolve.
-- `unique id` declares injectivity and `rel id mentor` keys the rel to it, so the hop is one index-of against the id column with one found-guard; the prime ids make every positional reading miss, so the resolution is proven, not coincident. The same hop runs before and after a despawn: not-found is dangling is dead — the ¯1 sentinel and the despawned target (id 11) fail the same guard, the left-join-null rule, no fault path. The keyed srel's image takes membership through its own key column, and the gamma count translates fiber keys to live rows, dropping dead members.
-- Statement order: gold lands pre-despawn on the two students of the dead master (ids 11, 13); post-despawn the same predicate strips Trained from id 13 alone (11 is gone); the image reaches ids 13 and 17; the reach count reads 2 live targets.
--! registry ../registries/015-keyed-hop.reg
--! expect-n 4
--! expect id = 7 13 17 19
--! expect gold = 0 100 0 0
--! expect trained = 1 0 1 1
--! expect frenzied = 0 1 1 0
--! expect reach = 2 0 0 0

Nord & mentor.Dead , Gold += 100
Cursed , ~
Nord & mentor.Dead , -Trained
Frenzy.targets' , +Frenzied
Frenzy , Reach = #/ targets'
